{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "citamedica-api-collection",
		"name": "CitaMedica API",
		"description": "Complete API collection for CitaMedica - Medical Appointment Management Platform\n\nThis collection includes all REST endpoints for managing patients, doctors, appointments, and webhooks.\n\n## Authentication\n\nMost endpoints require JWT authentication. Use the `/auth/login` endpoint to obtain a token, then set it in the `{{jwt_token}}` variable.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nCreate a Postman environment with these variables:\n- `base_url`: http://localhost:8080\n- `jwt_token`: (obtained from login)\n- `clinic_id`: 1\n- `doctor_id`: 1\n- `patient_id`: 1\n\n## Quick Start\n\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Create an environment with the variables above\n3. Run the \"Health Check\" request to verify the API is running\n4. Use \"Login\" to get a JWT token\n5. Explore other endpoints\n\nVersion: 1.0.0\nLast Updated: 2025-10-27",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Health & Monitoring",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Health Check",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/actuator/health",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"actuator",
								"health"
							]
						},
						"description": "Check the health status of the application and its dependencies (database, disk space, etc.)"
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "Health Check - UP",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "GET",
								"header": [],
